WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.856
Thermal imaging senses infrared radiation and displays apparent temperature patterns.

00:00:05.856 --> 00:00:14.258
It does not reveal hidden truth, identify exact causes, or operate like a visible-light photograph.

00:00:14.258 --> 00:00:24.188
Useful work depends on sensor type, resolution, sensitivity, lens, calibration context, distance, angle, target size, and environmental conditions.

00:00:24.188 --> 00:00:32.590
Time, sun, wind, moisture, material, reflections, geometry, and recent operating history can change the scene.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:40.992
Plan collection around a defined question, authorized area, useful contrast, stable coverage, safety, and privacy.

00:00:40.992 --> 00:00:46.339
Preserve original data, metadata, settings, conditions, and source links.

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:51.176
Interpret patterns against appropriate backgrounds and comparable components.

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:54.995
Separate observation, anomaly judgment, and diagnosis.

00:00:54.995 --> 00:01:02.379
Use calibrated confidence, identify alternative causes, and seek domain-specialist review for consequential findings.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:10.272
The goal is useful, defensible observation, not unsupported conclusions from colors on a screen.

00:01:10.272 --> 00:01:18.674
Strong thermal work combines planning, sensor awareness, environmental context, documentation, cautious reporting, and responsible use.
